<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liaoning</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liaoning is a province of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the Bohai Sea and the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shenyang">Shenyang</a>. Its lands, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-river">Liao River</a> plain and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> peninsula, were home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donghu">Donghu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> and other peoples and were contested by Chinese, Korean and steppe states. Shenyang, as Mukden, was the early capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a> before 1644.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liaoning.jpg" alt="Liaoning" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HSJ233 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xinghai_Square_.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
